WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.336 --> 00:00:18.298
Bill Sikes and Toby Crackit had abandoned him, Oliver lay unconscious in the ditch until early morning.

2
00:00:19.338 --> 00:00:21.819
At last a low cry of pain broke the stillness.

3
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.461
It was the day after the robbery and Oliver was awakening.

4
00:00:26.481 --> 00:00:30.183
His left arm, crudely bandaged in a shawl, hung heavy at his side.

5
00:00:31.123 --> 00:00:33.224
He was so weak that he could scarcely sit up.

6
00:00:34.156 --> 00:00:36.758
When he had done so, he looked feebly around for help.

7
00:00:37.778 --> 00:00:42.501
Trembling from cold and exhaustion, he made an effort to stand but fell back onto the ground.

8
00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:48.764
For a while he remained unconscious, but something within warned him that if he stayed there, he would

9
00:00:48.825 --> 00:00:49.485
surely die.

10
00:00:50.546 --> 00:00:52.787
So he struggled to his feet and stumbled forward.

11
00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:57.710
Staggering on, he crept over fences and through hedges until he came to a road.

12
00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.512
Here the rain began to fall so heavily that it roused him.

13
00:01:02.496 --> 00:01:04.658
He looked up and saw a house not far away.

14
00:01:05.579 --> 00:01:08.301
Perhaps the occupants would have pity on him and take him in.

15
00:01:10.042 --> 00:01:12.985
As he drew nearer, he felt that he had seen the house before.

16
00:01:13.866 --> 00:01:14.386
But where?

17
00:01:15.327 --> 00:01:16.388
Suddenly he remembered.

18
00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:19.631
It was the very house they had attempted to rob!

19
00:01:20.631 --> 00:01:23.414
Oliver knew he must flee, but he could scarcely stand.

20
00:01:24.415 --> 00:01:29.539
He climbed the front steps, knocked faintly at the door, and, with his strength failing him, sank down

21
00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:30.640
against a porch pillar.

22
00:01:31.752 --> 00:01:35.855
At that moment the two male servants who had gone out in pursuit of Oliver were entertaining the

23
00:01:35.915 --> 00:01:39.076
cook and the housemaid with the story of the previous night's adventures.

24
00:01:39.096 --> 00:01:43.119
"It was about half-past two when I woke up," said Mr.

25
00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:45.220
Giles, the butler, sipping tea in the kitchen.

26
00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.961
"I heard a noise."

27
00:01:48.042 --> 00:01:48.942
"What kind of noise?"

28
00:01:49.362 --> 00:01:49.943
asked the cook.

29
00:01:49.963 --> 00:01:53.885
"A noise like somebody was forcing open a door or a window.

30
00:01:55.006 --> 00:01:58.348
I decided to wake up Brittles and save him from being murdered in his bed."

31
00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:05.364
Here everyone looked at Brittles, who was still called the lad-of-all-work even though he was over thirty years

32
00:02:05.504 --> 00:02:08.926
old. "I tossed off my bedclothes," said Mr.

33
00:02:08.966 --> 00:02:14.890
Giles. "Then I got softly out of bed, put on a pair of—" "There are ladies present, Mr.

34
00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.251
Giles," warned Brittles.

35
00:02:16.271 --> 00:02:18.533
"A pair of shoes."

36
00:02:19.433 --> 00:02:22.295
Mr. Giles turned to him and laid great emphasis on the word.

37
00:02:22.315 --> 00:02:26.558
"Then I seized the loaded pistol that I always take upstairs at night.

38
00:02:27.579 --> 00:02:29.340
I walked on tiptoes to Brittles' room.

39
00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.902
'Brittles,' I said when I woke him, 'don't be frightened.'"

40
00:02:34.042 --> 00:02:35.003
"Was he frightened?"

41
00:02:35.423 --> 00:02:35.983
asked the cook.

42
00:02:37.164 --> 00:02:38.665
"Not a bit," replied Mr.

43
00:02:38.705 --> 00:02:43.607
Giles. "I would have died at once if it had been me," observed the housemaid.

44
00:02:43.627 --> 00:02:46.449
"You're a woman," said Brittles.

45
00:02:46.469 --> 00:02:48.390
"Brittles is right."

46
00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.091
Mr. Giles nodded his head approvingly.

47
00:02:52.892 --> 00:02:54.813
"Nothing else is to be expected from a woman.

48
00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:59.116
But being men, we took a lantern and groped our way downstairs."

49
00:03:00.224 --> 00:03:04.925
Mr. Giles had risen from his chair and taken two steps forward to demonstrate their actions when a

50
00:03:05.025 --> 00:03:06.706
sound startled everyone in the kitchen.

51
00:03:07.626 --> 00:03:09.207
The cook and the housemaid screamed.

52
00:03:10.307 --> 00:03:12.448
"It was a knock at the front door," said Mr.

53
00:03:12.468 --> 00:03:13.628
Giles, perfectly calm.

54
00:03:13.648 --> 00:03:15.789
"Open the door, somebody."

55
00:03:16.789 --> 00:03:17.529
Nobody moved.

56
00:03:17.549 --> 00:03:21.270
"A knock coming so early in the morning seems strange.

57
00:03:22.191 --> 00:03:23.751
But somebody must open the door."

58
00:03:24.711 --> 00:03:26.792
Mr. Giles looked at Brittles, who said nothing.

59
00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:32.084
"If Brittles would prefer to open the door in the presence of witnesses, I will be one," said

60
00:03:32.124 --> 00:03:32.824
Mr. Giles.

61
00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:36.307
Brittles went upstairs, followed by Mr.

62
00:03:36.347 --> 00:03:39.590
Giles and the two women, who were too frightened to stay behind in the kitchen.

63
00:03:40.671 --> 00:03:44.454
They talked loudly to warn any evil person outside that they were strong in number.

64
00:03:45.575 --> 00:03:48.297
Brittles opened the door while the others peeked over his shoulders.

65
00:03:49.298 --> 00:03:51.340
And there sat poor little Oliver Twist.

66
00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.222
"A boy!"

67
00:03:53.602 --> 00:03:54.202
exclaimed Mr.

68
00:03:54.222 --> 00:03:55.764
Giles, pushing Brittles aside.

69
00:03:56.692 --> 00:03:58.533
"Why, Brittles, do you know who this is?"

70
00:03:59.693 --> 00:04:02.455
Mr. Giles grabbed Oliver and lugged him into the front hall.

71
00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.776
"Here's one of the thieves, ma'am!"

72
00:04:05.156 --> 00:04:06.797
Mr. Giles called up the staircase.

73
00:04:06.817 --> 00:04:08.577
"He's wounded, miss!

74
00:04:08.978 --> 00:04:10.458
I shot him and Brittles held the light."

75
00:04:11.479 --> 00:04:14.820
The two female servants ran upstairs to carry the news to old Mrs.

76
00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:17.521
Maylie, the owner of the house, and her niece, Rose.

77
00:04:19.262 --> 00:04:23.144
Mr. Giles tried to revive Oliver so that he wouldn't die before he could be hanged.

78
00:04:24.244 --> 00:04:28.467
In the midst of all this commotion, a sweet female voice quieted everything in an instant.

79
00:04:28.487 --> 00:04:32.190
"Giles!" whispered Rose, a pretty young woman.

80
00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.251
"Don't be frightened, miss.

81
00:04:35.152 --> 00:04:36.973
He didn't make a very desperate resistance.

82
00:04:37.974 --> 00:04:39.174
I was soon too much for him."

83
00:04:39.194 --> 00:04:41.876
"Hush!" replied the young lady.

84
00:04:41.896 --> 00:04:44.978
"You frighten my aunt as much as the thieves did.

85
00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.440
Is the poor creature badly hurt?"

86
00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.582
"Wounded desperately."

87
00:04:49.602 --> 00:04:53.792
"He looks as if he is dying, miss," called Brittles.

88
00:04:53.812 --> 00:04:55.674
"Would you like to come and look at him in case he does?"

89
00:04:56.835 --> 00:04:58.537
Rose preferred to consult with her aunt.

90
00:04:59.417 --> 00:05:03.341
She soon returned to the top of the stairs with the instructions that the wounded person was to

91
00:05:03.361 --> 00:05:04.883
be carried carefully up to Mr.

92
00:05:04.903 --> 00:05:05.623
Giles' room.

93
00:05:07.365 --> 00:05:10.848
Brittles was ordered to ride to Chertsey and send for the doctor and a policeman.

94
00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:12.650
"Poor fellow!"

95
00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:15.893
said Rose as she refused yet another offer to look at the thief.

96
00:05:15.913 --> 00:05:19.036
"Oh, treat him kindly, Giles, for my sake."

97
00:05:20.096 --> 00:05:21.077
An hour later Dr.

98
00:05:21.097 --> 00:05:24.620
Losberne bustled into the room where Rose and her aunt were finishing breakfast.

99
00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.641
"My dear Mrs.

100
00:05:26.682 --> 00:05:29.184
Maylie! I never heard of such a thing!

101
00:05:30.084 --> 00:05:32.086
Breaking into a house in the middle of the night!"

102
00:05:32.446 --> 00:05:33.267
exclaimed the doctor.

103
00:05:33.287 --> 00:05:35.529
"You ought to be dead with fright!

104
00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:41.093
And you, Miss Rose—" "Yes, indeed," said Rose, interrupting him.

105
00:05:41.113 --> 00:05:45.137
"But there is a poor creature upstairs whom my aunt wishes you to see."

106
00:05:45.157 --> 00:05:47.138
"Ah, to be sure.

107
00:05:48.039 --> 00:05:48.960
Lead me to him, Giles.

108
00:05:49.984 --> 00:05:51.625
This was your handiwork, I understand."

109
00:05:52.726 --> 00:05:54.467
The doctor followed the butler upstairs.

110
00:05:56.228 --> 00:06:00.091
The doctor was absent much longer than either he or the ladies had anticipated.

111
00:06:01.152 --> 00:06:05.194
The servants ran up and down the stairs as a large box was fetched out of his carriage

112
00:06:05.294 --> 00:06:07.276
and the bedroom bell was rung very often.

113
00:06:08.477 --> 00:06:09.217
At last Dr.

114
00:06:09.257 --> 00:06:10.778
Losberne rejoined Rose and Mrs.

115
00:06:10.818 --> 00:06:14.541
Maylie. "This is a very extraordinary thing," he said.

116
00:06:14.561 --> 00:06:16.362
"Have you seen the thief?"

117
00:06:17.603 --> 00:06:18.663
"No," said Mrs.

118
00:06:20.044 --> 00:06:21.525
Maylie. "Then you should come with me at once."

119
00:06:22.565 --> 00:06:25.426
He offered one arm to Rose and held out his other hand to Mrs.

120
00:06:25.466 --> 00:06:29.028
Maylie. "I promise there's nothing alarming in his appearance."

121
00:06:30.228 --> 00:06:33.310
Leading them upstairs, he paused for a moment outside the bedroom.

122
00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:35.450
Then he threw open the door.

123
00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:37.491
"Oh, my!"

124
00:06:37.871 --> 00:06:38.292
said Mrs.

125
00:06:38.352 --> 00:06:40.953
Maylie. "He's only a boy!"

126
00:06:41.273 --> 00:06:42.053
gasped Rose.
